Links into the MariaDB extension open in the editor

Agents link to the MariaDB VS Code extension (MariaDB.mariadb-shell), for
example vscode://mariadb.mariadb-shell/msm/openDiagram?project=…&diagram=…
after creating an MSM project, so the user can open the result in one click.
The chat's Markdown blanked every href except http(s)/mailto, so the link was
dead.

Markdown lets an href through when its authority is mariadb.mariadb-shell,
whatever its scheme, and renders it like a session link: href="#" plus a
window event (mariadb:open-extension-link), inert outside interactive mode.
The VS Code companion forwards the event to the extension host
(openExtensionLink), which accepts only that authority, lower-cases it,
replaces the scheme with vscode.env.uriScheme (the agent can't know whether
the host is vscode, vscode-insiders or a Theia app) and keeps the rest of the
link as written. VS Code opens it with env.openExternal; Theia with
vscode.open, because Theia's openExternal hands its own scheme to the
operating system instead of the plugin's URI handler. Without an installed
handler the click does nothing, on purpose.

